{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It holds the same keys and answers the same queries as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", with the same names, but has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a vertex per key and per branching point rather than per symbol: O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":") vertices for ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":" keys,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"however long they are. That suits keys with long shared prefixes, such as file paths or URLs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Lookup, insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"d","type":"text"}]},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"text":") for a key of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"text":" symbols that passes ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"d"}]},{"text":" vertices of at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"text":" children.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let paths = RadixTree([\"\/usr\/bin\", \"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"])","paths.contains(\"\/usr\/lib\")                                   \/\/ true","paths.elements(withPrefix: \"\/usr\/l\").map { String($0) }      \/\/ [\"\/usr\/lib\", \"\/usr\/local\/bin\"]","paths.longestPrefix(of: \"\/usr\/bin\/swift\").map { String($0) } \/\/ \"\/usr\/bin\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, and the edge labels are slices of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer of symbols, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 vertices and label symbols, and copying"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/RadixTree.swift#L27","fileName":"RadixTree.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"}],"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"symbolKind